.TH EWVERIFY 1 "2026-07-11" "EW-Verify v0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ewverify \- Electronic Warfare Purple Team validation suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ewverify
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
EW-Verify is a Purple Team adversarial validation tool for Electronic Warfare detection capabilities on Linux. It runs controlled adversarial actions in the wireless and electromagnetic spectrum, then cross-references each one against the kernel and RF interfaces that detection tools rely on.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \--json
Export JSON report (silent mode, no banner)
.TP
.B \--csv
Export CSV report
.TP
.B \--deauth
Run deauthentication attack scenario
.TP
.B \--gps-spoof
Run GPS spoofing scenario
.TP
.B \--bt-attack
Run Bluetooth attack scenario
.TP
.B \--spectrum
Run spectrum congestion analysis
.TP
.B \--rfkill
Check RF kill switch state
.TP
.B \--regulatory
Check wireless regulatory domain
.TP
.B \--aireplay
Run aireplay-ng attack scenario
.TP
.B \--sdr
Check SDR device readiness
.TP
.B \--wifi-jam
Run Wi-Fi jamming scenario
.TP
.B \--channel-hop
Run channel hopping analysis
.TP
.B \--live
Invoke live detection tools for validation
.TP
.B \--verify-only
Read-only assessment (no attacks)
.TP
.B \--cleanup
Clean up remaining child processes
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Show version
